Fonts bundled with the TCI site
===============================

Two typefaces are self-hosted here rather than loaded from a CDN. Both are the
exact woff2 subsets that fonts.gstatic.com serves (latin and latin-ext, variable
weight axis), fetched on 2026-09-05 and committed unmodified.

  outfit-latin.woff2            Outfit, latin           wght 400-800
  outfit-latin-ext.woff2        Outfit, latin-ext       wght 400-800
  jetbrains-mono-latin.woff2    JetBrains Mono, latin   wght 400-600
  jetbrains-mono-latin-ext.woff2  JetBrains Mono, latin-ext  wght 400-600

WHY SELF-HOSTED
---------------
1. The site makes exactly zero off-origin requests, and a test enforces it
   (tests/test_site.py::test_pages_are_self_contained). Stylesheets are inlined
   and every graphic is SVG or DOM; a font <link> would be the only exception.
2. Embedding Google Fonts sends every visitor's IP address to a third party.
   For a benchmark administered from the EU that is an avoidable disclosure,
   and German courts have found the practice unlawful under the GDPR
   (LG Munchen I, 3 O 17493/20, 20 January 2022).
3. The Vercel and GitHub Pages mirrors must serve byte-identical pages under a
   strict CSP. A same-origin font file satisfies both; a CDN reference does not.

Rendering is identical either way: same files, same unicode-ranges, same
variable axes. Only the host changes.

